A log of creating an Operating System. Or at least, bits and pieces of an operating system.


HOW TO:
The OS includes a Makefile that, if exported, should run under the commands presuming the user is in the same folder that the makefile exists under:
make clean
make
make run

## KNOWN LIMITATIONS

### Keyboard Support

The keyboard driver currently targets older PS/2-style keyboards and does not support USB keyboards. As a result, booting EquineOS directly on physical hardware from a USB device may not work without additional configuration.

The ISO image has been tested successfully in virtual machines.

### Doom Resources

For licensing reasons, the public build does not include `doom1_wad.h`.

This file is a generated C header containing Doom WAD game data, created by converting a legally obtained WAD file into a C-compatible resource. It is referenced by the Doom `stdio.c` file.

A dummy replacement header is included instead.

Users who wish to run Doom must provide their own legally obtained WAD file and regenerate the resource file.

### Bad Apple Resources

The public build does not include the original Bad Apple animation data.

The Bad Apple application converts animation frames into binary data. The included build uses a demonstration resource containing placeholder data.

Only animation data is included. Audio is not included.

## SPECIAL THANKS

### doomgeneric

EquineOS includes a port of doomgeneric using the C files and headers provided by the project.

Source:
https://github.com/ozkl/doomgeneric

License:
GNU General Public License v2.0

### font8x8

EquineOS uses font8x8 for bitmap font data.

Source:
https://github.com/dhepper/font8x8/blob/master/font8x8_basic.h

License:
Public Domain

---

EquineOS does not distribute Doom WAD files or Bad Apple animation resources.
